{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1004,"nextCursorMark":"AoIIPVa8nSc4MTI4ODM5","nextPageUrl":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=SRC%3AMED+AND+%28TITLE_ABS%3Aosteoclast*+OR+TITLE_ABS%3A%22bone+resorption%22%29+AND+%28TITLE_ABS%3ASRC+OR+TITLE_ABS%3AVAV3+OR+TITLE_ABS%3Acortactin+OR+TITLE_ABS%3A%22sealing+zone%22+OR+TITLE_ABS%3Apodosome*%29&cursorMark=AoIIPVa8nSc4MTI4ODM5&resultType=core&pageSize=500&format=json","request":{"queryString":"SRC:MED AND (TITLE_ABS:osteoclast* OR TITLE_ABS:\"bone resorption\") AND (TITLE_ABS:SRC OR TITLE_ABS:VAV3 OR TITLE_ABS:cortactin OR TITLE_ABS:\"sealing zone\" OR TITLE_ABS:podosome*)","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"AoIIPWEfkSc5MzU4ODI5","pageSize":500,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"2629823","source":"MED","pmid":"2629823","title":"Podosome expression in osteoclasts: influence of high extracellular calcium concentration.","authorString":"Teti A, Barattolo R, Grano M, Colucci S, Argentino L, Teitelbaum SL, Hruska KA, Santacroce G, Zambonin Zallone A.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Teti A","lastName":"Teti","firstName":"A","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Barattolo R","lastName":"Barattolo","firstName":"R","initials":"R"},{"fullName":"Grano M","lastName":"Grano","firstName":"M","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Colucci S","lastName":"Colucci","firstName":"S","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Argentino L","lastName":"Argentino","firstName":"L","initials":"L"},{"fullName":"Teitelbaum SL","lastName":"Teitelbaum","firstName":"S L","initials":"SL","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4054-6679"}},{"fullName":"Hruska KA","lastName":"Hruska","firstName":"K A","initials":"KA"},{"fullName":"Santacroce G","lastName":"Santacroce","firstName":"G","initials":"G"},{"fullName":"Zambonin Zallone A","lastName":"Zambonin Zallone","firstName":"A","initials":"A"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4054-6679"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"11","volume":"65","journalIssueId":732739,"dateOfPublication":"1989 Nov","monthOfPublication":11,"yearOfPublication":1989,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Boll Soc Ital Biol Sper","title":"Bollettino della Societa italiana di biologia sperimentale","essn":"2284-0230","issn":"0037-8771","nlmid":"7506962","isoabbreviation":"Boll Soc Ital Biol Sper"},"printPublicationDate":"1989-11-01"},"pubYear":"1989","pageInfo":"1039-1043","abstractText":"In this study the effect of high extracellular calcium concentration has been evaluated, by immunofluorescence, on podosome expression in chicken osteoclasts. Cells were cultured in presence of 0.2 and 4 mM calcium for 90 minutes and microfilaments were detected, after fixation and permeabilization, by decoration with rodhamine conjugated phalloidin. Results showed that increased extracellular calcium concentration induces the inhibition of podosome expression indicating that these close-contact areas are capable of calcium-mediated regulation.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cells, Cultured"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Osteoclasts","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"DE","qualifierName":"drug effects"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Chickens"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Calcium","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PD","qualifierName":"pharmacology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cell Adhesion","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}}]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Calcium","registryNumber":"SY7Q814VUP"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":3,"hasReferences":"N","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"1990-05-01","dateOfCreation":"1989-11-01","dateOfRevision":"2013-11-21","firstPublicationDate":"1989-11-01","firstIndexDate":"2008-01-29","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"2597415","source":"MED","pmid":"2597415","title":"Regulation of podosomes by intracellular pH in avian osteoclasts.","authorString":"Teti A, Grano M, Teitelbaum SL, Hruska KA, Colucci S, Zambonin Zallone A.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Teti A","lastName":"Teti","firstName":"A","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Grano M","lastName":"Grano","firstName":"M","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Teitelbaum SL","lastName":"Teitelbaum","firstName":"S L","initials":"SL","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4054-6679"}},{"fullName":"Hruska KA","lastName":"Hruska","firstName":"K A","initials":"KA"},{"fullName":"Colucci S","lastName":"Colucci","firstName":"S","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Zambonin Zallone A","lastName":"Zambonin Zallone","firstName":"A","initials":"A"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4054-6679"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"7","volume":"65","journalIssueId":710169,"dateOfPublication":"1989 Jul","monthOfPublication":7,"yearOfPublication":1989,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Boll Soc Ital Biol Sper","title":"Bollettino della Societa italiana di biologia sperimentale","essn":"2284-0230","issn":"0037-8771","nlmid":"7506962","isoabbreviation":"Boll Soc Ital Biol Sper"},"printPublicationDate":"1989-07-01"},"pubYear":"1989","pageInfo":"597-601","abstractText":"The effects of changes in intracellular pH (pH1) on the organization of the clear zone of isolated avian osteoclasts in culture were studied. The distribution of podosomes, the close contact areas that mediate the adhesion of osteoclasts to the substrate, was investigated by decoration of microfilaments with fluorescent phalloidin. Intracellular acidification by butyric acid induces significant increase of podosome formation at the level of the clear zone compared to controls. Conversely, alkalinization by HCO3- reduces the percentage of osteoclasts with podosomes. A role of pH1 on the adhesion of the osteoclasts to the substrate is hypothesized.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cells, Cultured"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Microbodies","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Osteoclasts","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CY","qualifierName":"cytology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Birds"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cell Adhesion"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Hydrogen-Ion Concentration"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":5,"hasReferences":"N","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"1990-02-07","dateOfCreation":"1989-07-01","dateOfRevision":"2003-11-14","firstPublicationDate":"1989-07-01","firstIndexDate":"2008-01-29","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"2542071","source":"MED","pmid":"2542071","doi":"10.1016/0014-4827(89)90266-8","title":"Immunocytochemical distribution of extracellular matrix receptors in human osteoclasts: a beta 3 integrin is colocalized with vinculin and talin in the podosomes of osteoclastoma giant cells.","authorString":"Zambonin-Zallone A, Teti A, Grano M, Rubinacci A, Abbadini M, Gaboli M, Marchisio PC.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Zambonin-Zallone A","lastName":"Zambonin-Zallone","firstName":"A","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Istituto di Anatomia Umana Normale, Università di Bari, Italy."}]}},{"fullName":"Teti A","lastName":"Teti","firstName":"A","initials":"A","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5887-4419"}},{"fullName":"Grano M","lastName":"Grano","firstName":"M","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7121-5899"}},{"fullName":"Rubinacci A","lastName":"Rubinacci","firstName":"A","initials":"A","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1736-0531"}},{"fullName":"Abbadini M","lastName":"Abbadini","firstName":"M","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Gaboli M","lastName":"Gaboli","firstName":"M","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1600-0916"}},{"fullName":"Marchisio PC","lastName":"Marchisio","firstName":"P C","initials":"PC"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1600-0916"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5887-4419"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7121-5899"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1736-0531"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"2","volume":"182","journalIssueId":662336,"dateOfPublication":"1989 Jun","monthOfPublication":6,"yearOfPublication":1989,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Exp Cell Res","title":"Experimental cell research","essn":"1090-2422","issn":"0014-4827","nlmid":"0373226","isoabbreviation":"Exp Cell Res"},"printPublicationDate":"1989-06-01"},"pubYear":"1989","pageInfo":"645-652","abstractText":"Human osteoclasts (OCLs) obtained from cell suspensions of surgically excised giant cell bone tumors (osteoclastomas) were attached to glass coverslips and analyzed by immunofluorescence with antibodies to integrins and cytoskeletal proteins. It was found that in OCLs (i) podosomes, identified by their F-actin core and by interference reflection microscopy, were predominantly found in a peripheral belt as described in avian OCLs; (ii) each F-actin core was surrounded by a ring of vinculin and talin; (iii) beta 1 integrin was diffuse in the ventral membrane; (iv) beta 3 integrin was distributed in intensely fluorescent rings surrounding F-actin cores; (v) beta 2 integrin was absent; (vi) beta 4 integrin was absent. The macrophages detected in the same coverslips displayed podosomes containing beta 2 but not beta 3, fibroblasts showed adhesion plaques positive for beta 1 and beta 3 but not for beta 2, and platelets were intensely positive for beta 3. These results indicate that OCLs produce an integrin complex that is absent in the monocyte-macrophage lineage.","affiliation":"Istituto di Anatomia Umana Normale, Università di Bari, Italy.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Tumor Cells, Cultured","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CY","qualifierName":"cytology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Extracellular Matrix","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"UL","qualifierName":"ultrastructure"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Osteoclasts","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PA","qualifierName":"pathology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"UL","qualifierName":"ultrastructure"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Giant Cell Tumors","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PA","qualifierName":"pathology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Bone Neoplasms","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PA","qualifierName":"pathology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorNa